# Mod packages (built artifacts, too large for git)
*.ccpmod

# DroneMod contents distributed separately (avatars, sounds, scripts, etc.)
ConditioningControlPanel/DroneMod/*

# ...except the canonical drone-mode.ccpmod package, which is shipped as a
# bundled built-in mod (see ConditioningControlPanel.csproj + ModService.ExtractBundledBuiltInMods).
!ConditioningControlPanel/DroneMod/drone-mode.ccpmod

# ...and the Locked mode resources bundle, likewise shipped as a bundled
# built-in mod (see ConditioningControlPanel.csproj + ModService.ExtractBundledResourceMods).
!ConditioningControlPanel/LockedMod/locked-resources.ccpmod

# MSBuild temp files
*_wpftmp.csproj

# Environment and secrets
*.env
*.env.*
nul

# Avatar-emote production tooling (private generation pipeline — Kling prompts,
# seeds, scratch GIFs). The produced Resources\*_emotes\ assets ARE committed; the
# scripts that make them are not. See tools/avatar-emotes/README.md (local only).
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED 2026-08-14. This was a bare `tools/`, which git matches at ANY depth,
# so it silently swallowed `client/tools/` as well. The 18 files already tracked there
# survived only because they predate the rule — every NEW file under client/tools/ was
# being ignored, which is how the multi-lane gate and wave tooling nearly shipped as
# untracked and would have vanished from every lane worktree. The rule only ever meant
# the root-level private pipeline its own comment names.
/tools/

# ...except the Bureau pack-indexer (builds packs-index.json / bureau-catalogue.json
# for the labeling game — no secrets, meant to be re-runnable by anyone).
!ConditioningControlPanel/tools/
ConditioningControlPanel/tools/*
!ConditioningControlPanel/tools/pack-indexer/

# Redistributables (re-downloadable from Microsoft; do not bloat the repo).
# VC_redist.x64.exe is 25 MB and build-installer.bat fetches it on demand.
redist/

.worktrees/
# ...except the WebView2 Evergreen bootstrapper, which IS committed: 1.6 MB, and
# WebView2 is now load-bearing for FYP, Exclusives, DtRH, Goon Game and the default
# video engine, so an installer build must never silently skip it because a download
# failed. Official Microsoft fwlink: https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/p/?LinkId=2124703
!redist/
redist/*
!redist/MicrosoftEdgeWebview2Setup.exe

# Node tooling for local automation scripts (puppeteer-core for /x-drafts + capture
# work). Local-only; nothing in the shipped app uses node.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

# Marketing pipeline (/x-drafts) - ENTIRELY local, never publish.
# origin is a PUBLIC repo. archive-index.json embeds the Windows username in ~75 paths and
# describes explicit screenshots; topics.json describes unannounced features. Media is large
# and some of it is suggestive. Nothing in here belongs on GitHub.
marketing/
